# Firebox: out-of-repo build products written into the CLONE ROOT.
#
# The firebox build clone lives AT scripts/wasix-libc/build, so a script writing
# to "${SCRIPT_DIR}/build/libcxx-pic-build" lands at <clone>/libcxx-pic-build —
# the clone's ROOT, not a build/ dir inside it. The bare `build` entry above
# cannot reach those, so a completed libc build left the tree untracked-dirty
# and the firebox#HMS currency gate refused every render after the first
# (correctly: it cannot tell our own output from a stray source drop).
#
# Globs, not a list of what exists today: build-libcxx-{pic,ehpic}.sh generate
# the -build/-out pair per variant, so a NEW variant is covered on arrival.
# An untracked *source* file still reads dirty — the gate keeps its teeth.
/libcxx-*-build/
/libcxx-*-out/
/picthin/
